  "title": "The base dynamics conserve one local quantity exactly",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "ffd3b054-e942-43e1-b7f1-fca113ec5183",
      "text": "At the base of physics, one local quantity is conserved exactly: it is moved around but never created or destroyed. The frameworks that say so name different quantities: a continuous temporal current on spacetime, or the sum of discrete tones on a mesh.",
